    "body": "I placed the starship init commands inside a separate file placed in `$ZSH_CUSTOM/starship.zsh`\r\n\r\n```zsh\r\n# Set the config directory\r\nexport STARSHIP_CONFIG=~/dotfiles/starship/starship.toml\r\n# Load Starship prompt\r\neval \"$(starship init zsh)\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Update:** It's not a bug with Starship, I turned everything off but the terminal reports a non-zero exit state on startup. Starship is showing the right colors, something is wrong with my terminal configuration.\r\n<img width=\"1082\" alt=\"Screenshot 2022-02-25 at 12 31 51 PM\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/16580576/155682075-fb1c6224-7e05-41aa-97bf-6ef165bd162e.png\">\r\n\r\n**Update:** After further debugging, I found that `rvm` had left a stray line in `~/.zlogin` that was found using `set +x`. Removing it fixed everything. Thanks!",
